       | assistantfinalThe move replaces a number \(m\) by the sum of the digits of its base‑\(b\) expansion,
       | \[
       | S_b(m)=\sum_{k}a_k ,\qquad 
       | m=\sum_{k}a_k b^{\,k},\qquad 0\le a_k<b .
       | \]
       | 
       | --------------------------------------------------------------------
       | ### 1.  Largest possible next number
       | 
       | For a fixed \(m\) and a base \(b\,(2\le b\le m)\),
       | 
       | \[
       | S_b(m)\le (b-1)\bigl(\lfloor\log_b m\rfloor+1\bigr) .
       | \]
       | 
       | If we write \(m=q\,b+r\;(0\le r<b)\) we have  
       | \(S_b(m)=S_b(q)+r\le (b-1)(\lfloor\log_b q\rfloor+2)\).
       | 
       | Choosing \(b=\bigl\lfloor\frac{m}{2}\bigr\rfloor+1\) gives a two‑digit representation  
       | 
       | \[
       | m=1\cdot b+(m-b),\qquad 0\le m-b<b .
       | \]
       | 
       | Hence  
       | 
       | \[
       | S_b(m)=1+(m-b)=\Bigl\lceil\frac{m}{2}\Bigr\rceil .
       | \]
       | 
       | One checks that no larger sum is possible, so
       | 
       | \[
       | \boxed{\,\max_{2\le b\le m}S_b(m)=\bigl\lceil \tfrac{m}{2}\bigr\rceil\, } .
       | \]
       | 
       | --------------------------------------------------------------------
       | ### 2.  Longest possible chain
       | 
       | Let \(f(m)\) be the maximal number of moves that can be performed starting
       | from \(m\) (with \(f(1)=0\)).  
       | From the result above we obtain the recurrence
       | 
       | \[
       | f(m)=1+f\!\left(\Bigl\lceil\frac{m}{2}\Bigr\rceil\right),\qquad m>1 .
       | \]
       | 
       | Induction shows  
       | 
       | \[
       | f(m)=\Bigl\lceil\log_2 m\Bigr\rceil .
       | \]
       | 
       | Indeed after \(t\) steps the value is \(\bigl\lceil m/2^{\,t}\bigr\rceil\);
       | the first time this equals \(1\) is when \(2^{\,t}\ge m\), i.e.  
       | \(t=\lceil\log_2 m\rceil\).
       | 
       | Thus for any starting integer \(n\)
       | 
       | \[
       | \text{maximum moves from }n = \lceil\log_2 n\rceil .
       | \]
       | 
