       | \[
       | \mathcal F=\{\alpha:\mathbb Z\to\mathbb Z\;|\;\alpha (n)=0\text{ for all but finitely many }n\}.
       | \]
       | 
       | For \(\alpha ,\beta\in\mathcal F\)
       | 
       | \[
       | \alpha\star\beta=\sum_{n\in\mathbb Z}\alpha (n)\beta (n)
       | \]
       | 
       | and the shift operator  
       | 
       | \[
       | S_{m}(\alpha)(t)=\alpha(t+m).
       | \]
       | 
       | --------------------------------------------------------------------
       | ### 1.  Polynomial description  
       | 
       | Write  
       | 
       | \[
       | A(x)=\sum_{i=0}^{8}\alpha(i)x^{i}\in\mathbb Z[x] .
       | \]
       | 
       | Because \(\alpha(m)=0\) for \(m<0\) and \(m>8\), the support of \(\alpha\) is contained in
       | \(\{0,1,\dots ,8\}\); thus \(A\) is a polynomial of degree \(\le 8\).
       | 
       | For any \(\beta\in\mathcal F\) put  
       | 
       | \[
       | \Gamma (x)=\sum_{t\in\mathbb Z}\beta(t)x^{t}\in\mathbb Z[x,x^{-1}]
       | \]
       | 
       | (Laurent polynomial).  
       | A direct change of index shows
       | 
       | \[
       | S_{n}(\alpha)\star\beta=\sum_{t}\alpha(t+n)\beta(t)
       |       =\bigl(A(x)x^{\,n}\bigr)\star\beta
       |       =\bigl(A(x)\Gamma (x)\bigr)_{x^{\,n}},
       | \]
       | 
       | i.e. the coefficient of \(x^{n}\) in the product \(A(x)\Gamma (x)\).
       | 
       | Hence the condition in the definition of a *shifty* function is
       | 
       | \[
       | \exists\;k\neq l\in\mathbb Z,\;\exists\;\Gamma (x)\in\mathbb Z[x,x^{-1}]
       | \quad\text{such that}\quad
       | A(x)\Gamma (x)=x^{k}+x^{l}. \tag{1}
       | \]
       | 
       | --------------------------------------------------------------------
       | ### 2.  Reduction to a divisor of \(1+x^{d}\)
       | 
       | Write \(k\le l\) and put \(d=l-k>0\).  
       | Equation (1) becomes  
       | 
       | \[
       | A(x)\Gamma (x)=x^{k}\bigl(1+x^{d}\bigr).
       | \]
       | 
       | Since a monomial \(x^{k}\) is a unit in the Laurent ring,
       | \(A(x)\) must divide \(1+x^{d}\) in \(\mathbb Z[x,x^{-1}]\).
       | 
       | Let  
       | 
       | \[
       | r=\min\{i\mid\alpha(i)\neq0\},\qquad
       | B(x)=x^{-r}A(x).
       | \]
       | 
       | Then \(B(0)=\pm1\) and  
       | 
       | \[
       | B(x)\mid 1+x^{d}\qquad\text{in }\mathbb Z[x].
       | \tag{2}
       | \]
       | 
